  "body": "## What changed\n\nMCP read modes for small context windows (`crates/app/src/mcp/`):\n\n- `get_job` takes `summary: true`. The summary removes `machine.definition`. Each operation keeps only the `params` fields that differ from the kind defaults. Null and empty fields outside `params` are removed.\n- `list_operation_types` takes `kind` (key or label) and `section`. An unknown name is refused with the valid names.\n- `list_features` takes `compact: true`. Compact rows keep the id, the name and the pick facts. Counts replace the loops. The compact default `limit` is 25. The full default stays 500.\n- `provider::tools_in(provider, ToolSet::Core)` gives a core set of 25 workflow tools. `tools(provider)` is unchanged.\n- The new code is in `mcp/compact.rs`. `job.rs`, `features.rs`, `pick.rs` and `tools.rs` get small hooks only.\n\nChat worker limits (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/ai_chat/budget.rs`):\n\n- A tool reply to the model is cut at 12000 JSON characters, with a hint that names the compact modes. The tool card keeps the full text.\n- A request carries at most one viewport image (the newest).\n- A turn stops after 12 model rounds. The old `MAX_TURN_STEPS` moved to `budget::MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS` and now has a test.\n- A request carries at most 6 earlier turns. When older turns are dropped, the latest `get_job` reply goes in front of the first kept prompt.\n- A local endpoint gets the core tool set. A cloud endpoint gets the full table.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/1944-ai-context-budgets.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nEnhancement. The full tool table and one full `get_job` or `list_features` reply can fill the context window of a small local model.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe results in this section apply to original head `398a4a937a6267dce87da97495149713412920a5`.\nThe final-head results are in \"Latest review findings\" below.\n\nPins (all new; network is not used):\n\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_compact.rs`: `get_job_summary_drops_the_machine_definition_and_default_fields`, `get_job_summary_refuses_a_non_boolean`, `list_operation_types_filters_by_kind_and_by_section`, `list_features_compact_rows_are_short_and_the_default_limit_is_chat_sized`, `the_core_tool_set_is_a_small_subset_of_the_full_table`. Each asserts a character budget.\n- `egui_app::tests::ai_chat::budget`: `a_long_tool_reply_is_cut_to_the_character_cap_with_a_hint`, `a_local_model_gets_the_core_tool_set_and_a_cloud_model_the_full_table`, `a_turn_stops_at_the_round_cap`.\n- `egui_app::ai_chat::budget::tests`: `a_cut_keeps_whole_characters_and_says_how_much_was_shown`, `a_small_reply_passes_and_a_long_one_is_one_capped_text_block`, `only_the_newest_image_goes_with_a_request`, `old_turns_are_dropped_and_the_latest_get_job_reply_is_kept`.\n\nMutation checks (old code put back, pin red; code restored, pin green):\n\n- `job.rs` from upstream: the two `get_job` pins and the `list_operation_types` pin are red.\n- `features.rs` from upstream: the `list_features` pin is red.\n- Core filter turned off in `provider.rs`: the core set pin is red.\n- `worker_mcp.rs` from upstream: the reply cap pin is red.\n- `turn.rs` from upstream: the image pin and the history pin are red.\n- `tool_set_for` gives `Full` to local: the tool set pin is red.\n- Loop runs `MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS + 1`: the round cap pin is red.\n\nOriginal-head gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed (131 steps, 0 failed). Original-head clippy passed. That head later conflicted with upstream main. The final-head results below replace these results.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No posted G-code changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A real provider endpoint. The tests use the scripted transport.\n- The `camcraft-mcp` skill does not list the new arguments yet. The tool schemas describe them.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThese open PRs touch the same files, in different functions or lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\n- #2836: `list_operation_types` (a field inside the loop; this PR changes the signature and the end).\n- #2920 and #2716: `features.rs` views and `list_features`; `tools.rs` `list_features` row (this PR adds three lines in `list_features` and edits the `get_job` and `list_operation_types` rows).\n- #2554, #2678, #2773: other rows and functions of `job.rs` and `tools.rs`.\n\nChangelog: AI chat keeps large jobs inside the model's context: compact MCP read modes (`get_job` summary, `list_operation_types` kind/section filter, `list_features` compact), a core tool set for local models, and caps on tool reply size, images, rounds and history.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #1944\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n## Latest review findings\n\nHead: `3c4a0b37c2cf662fe1a2cae9004a23a8135aa088`.\n\n- The merge from upstream main keeps the importer warning for edges that lie off their surfaces. It also keeps the compact schemas. `tool_advertisements_keep_import_fidelity_guidance_and_job_summary` pins both tool entries. Reverting each part makes the pin fail. Restoring both parts makes it pass.\n- The before and after images below show the same offline chat request: `List the operation kinds`. The full tool card remains visible in both images. The model reply decreases from 67,669 to 10,674 characters. The visible tool card keeps all 67,669 characters. The images are identical because the panel retains the full reply. `a_long_tool_reply_is_cut_to_the_character_cap_with_a_hint` checks the model request. The before capture uses `worker_mcp.rs` from parent `398a4a937^`. The after capture uses the final dispatch code. The temporary capture harness is not committed. All images are on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n- Final-head quick gate: `GREEN: 133 steps, 0 failed; 2,341 tests passed, 0 failed, 16 ignored; 15.8 minutes`.\n- Final-head clippy for `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui`: `GREEN: cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings; exit 0; 2 minutes 5 seconds`.\n- Final-head heavy gate: `GREEN: 201 steps, 0 failed; 41 tests passed; six existing known-fail pins failed as expected; 45.2 minutes`. Reached lanes: `app heavy targets selected by cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main, against upstream main f85163b0ca948250fd6a51360d14754a282e0340`.\n\n| Before | After |\n|---|---|\n| ![Before: full chat tool card](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/70d1393f2a68fc999f762faa20c3db9b86fbd104/3033/before.png) | ![After: full chat tool card retained](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/70d1393f2a68fc999f762faa20c3db9b86fbd104/3033/after.png) |\n\n\nThe heavy gate treats these existing known-fail pins as expected failures.\nThey are not failed gate steps. No unexpected heavy test failed.\n\n- [#2845](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/2845): `no_pickable_edge_is_a_tangent_piece_of_a_longer_one_in_any_step_fixture`; `solids_that_touch_face_to_face_are_two_outward_bodies`.\n- [#2849](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/2849): `an_axis_aligned_lead_start_posts_the_users_arc_entry_as_g18_or_g19`; `the_horizontal_arc_entry_on_the_users_pocket_verifies_silent`; `fig8_outside_containment_with_em0800_and_clearing_kinds_works`.\n- [#1950](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/1950): `the_users_whole_model_bore_roughs_adaptive_on_each_level`.\n",
